# .zolo — NOT YAML: string-first, no quotes needed, indentation-only nesting.
#> dev/flow spark — NOT a first-class app entry point. Jumps zRaven straight
#  to Register (zBlock: Register, zVaFile: zUI.Register), skipping the
#  Main→Register nav hop, so the verify-email flow doesn't pay the full
#  50-step canonical journey's nav tax every --run (13_testing.md dev_spark).
#
#  ALSO sidesteps a real core gap found running this flow inside the
#  canonical raven: session["_current_block_data"] (the %data.* stash a
#  zSpool resolves into) is never invalidated across zLogout/zLogin, so a
#  SECOND identity visiting Profile in the SAME long-lived zOS process can
#  still render the FIRST identity's stashed row. A dedicated dev spark
#  boots its OWN fresh process per --run — Charlie is the only person who
#  EVER visits Profile in this process's lifetime, so the stash starts
#  empty and the pre-existing bug never triggers. The bug itself is real
#  and worth a core fix (zLoom binding_ops.py `prepare_block_render` /
#  zGuard's Bifrost SPA nav seam) — reported separately, not patched here. <#

zSpark:
    title:     zRM — Verify Email (dev flow)
    zMode:     zBifrost
    zLog:      DEBUG
    zLogPath:  @.logs
    zVaFolder: @.zViews
    zVaFile:   zUI.Register
    zBlock:    Register
    zServer:
        enabled: true
